// Imported from the rev 474 cache by tools/models/importnpc474batch.py: models copied
// byte-for-byte, chatheads brought across, and one copy of each model shared between
// every npc that wears it. Combat stats, huntmode and drops are by hand - the cache
// carries none of them.
// The God Wars Dungeon cast, rev 474 (tools/models/importnpc474batch.py, batches/batch_gwd_cast.tsv).
// The four bosses are elsewhere - graardor.npc, kril.npc, zilyana.npc, kreearra.npc. This is everyone between you and them: twelve bodyguards, each god's warrior/ranger/mage, and the fifteen Aviansies.
// Combat stats are NOT in the cache and are not here yet; vislevel is the cache's own. Attack, defend and death animations are deliberately absent - see the batch file.

// Attack, defend and death, derived per RIG rather than guessed per npc - the cache states ready
// and walk and nothing else, which is why they were left out of the import.
//
// WHAT DECIDES IT: death is the priority-10 sequence, which is unambiguous on every rig and is
// also the longest. Attack is the priority-6 one carrying reachforward - the flag that makes the
// model lean into its target, which a block does not do. Defend is the priority-6 one left over.
//
// The method was checked against a rig this build had already named by hand: on the demon rig,
// 474 seq 64 carries the attack markers and is demon_attack, 65 is demon_block and the
// priority-10 67 is demon_death. It picks out what somebody else had already picked out.
//
// Three rigs needed nothing converted at all: the Zamorak and Saradomin spiritual npcs are on the
// human skeleton and take the human_sword_* set every other humanoid in the tree uses; the three
// Zamorak bodyguards are demons; and the Bandos spiritual npcs share General Graardor's own rig,
// so they swing what he swings.

